118089249e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.007251845672726631,0.0,-7.152555099310121e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0003045333724003285,-0.011304848827421665,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.0012276978231966496,-0.0017761897761374712,-7.748573807475623e-06,-3.1470757676288486e-05,0.0,0.0,-0.0004996005445718765,0.0,-0.05950954928994179,-0.00014578233822248876,-2.0265558760002023e-06,-1.7762025890988298e-05,-3.6954811548639555e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,1555,5733,1506,553,198,59,26056,10374,13233,90,85,92,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,220,16,488,259,24984,220,18,83,24984,220,16,481,259,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,60,48101,304,264,11031,315,279,1352,400,87,488,379,488,17988,284,294,2418,220,11252,279,11457,6716,4930,66,11991,568,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe line parameterized by\n\\[\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix}\\]lies in a plane of the form $x + y + cz = d.$  Enter the ordered pair $(c,d).$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"85b1c0e331e0ed798c0aaa2afa1023706b9842ceaf3f9ed294ff88558bb5b7c1"},"seconds":24.993433475494385,"seed":413908291469203337,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we will substitute the parametric equations of the line into the equation of the plane to find the values of \\(c\\) and \\(d\\).\n\nGiven the parametric form of the line:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 + t \\\\ 3t \\\\ 1 - t \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\nthe coordinates \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) of the line can be expressed as:\n\\[\nx = 1 + t, \\quad y = 3t, \\quad z = 1 - t.\n\\]\n\nThe equation of the plane is given by:\n\\[\nx + y + cz = d.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the parametric equations into the plane equation, we get:\n\\[\n(1 + t) + 3t + c(1 - t) = d.\n\\]\n\nSimplify the left-hand side:\n\\[\n1 + t + 3t + c - ct = d.\n\\]\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n1 + c + (1 + 3 - c)t = d.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n1 + c + (4 - c)t = d.\n\\]\n\nFor the line to lie in the plane, the equation \\(1 + c + (4 - c)t = d\\) must hold for all values of \\(t\\). This implies that the coefficient of \\(t\\) must be zero (since the equation must be independent of \\(t\\)):\n\\[\n4 - c = 0.\n\\]\nSolving for \\(c\\):\n\\[\nc = 4.\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\(c = 4\\) back into the equation to find \\(d\\):\n\\[\n1 + 4 = d,\n\\]\n\\[\nd = 5.\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair \\((c, d)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(4, 5)}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{(4, 5)}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
